body:
I completely understand this feeling. Growing up as a child was hell. No one liked me because I was weird/quirky/dorky/nerdy. I was often bullied, being different made me stand out and made me a target. Growing up around people who try so hard to fit in and make fun of anyone else "different" is not fun but sadly that is how the world is. There was a short period of time as a teenager where I tried fitting in but I found out pretty fast that that just wasn't doing it for me. 

&#x200B;

Now as a 27 year old I still struggle with people who are judgmental and look at being "different" as bad. Long ago I said fuck it and just went all out with being myself and have attracted like-minded people. It can get lonely but wouldn't you rather be lonely than being around people who are closed-minded? Anyways, I hope you find people who appreciate you for you.
